open pore conformation of potassium channels. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>417</volume>:<fpage>523</fpage>&#x02013;526.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12037560</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Jiang, Y., A. Lee, J. Chen, V. Ruta, M. Cadene, B.T. Chait, and R. MacKinnon. <year>2003</year>. X-ray structure of a voltage-dependent K&#x0002b; channel. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>423</volume>:<fpage>33</fpage>&#x02013;41.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12721618</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Jiang, Y., A. Pico, M. Cadene, B.T. Chait, and R. MacKinnon. <year>2001</year>. Structure of the RCK domain from the <italic>E. coli</italic> K&#x0002b; channel and demonstration of its presence in the human BK channel. <source>Neuron.</source> <volume>29</volume>:<fpage>593</fpage>&#x02013;601.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11301020</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Kaupp, U.B., and R. Seifert. <year>2001</year>. Molecular diversity of pacemaker ion channels. <source>Annu. Rev. Physiol.</source> <volume>63</volume>:<fpage>235</fpage>&#x02013;257.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11181956</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Kaupp, U.B., and R. Seifert. <year>2002</year>. Cyclic nucleotide-gated ion channels. <source>Physiol. Rev.</source> <volume>82</volume>:<fpage>769</fpage>&#x02013;824.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12087135</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Kohler, M., B. Hirschberg, C.T. Bond, J.M. Kinzie, N.V. Marrion, J. Maylie, and J.P. Adelman. <year>1996</year>. Small-conductance, calcium-activated potassium channels from mammalian brain. <source>Science.</source> <volume>273</volume>:<fpage>1709</fpage>&#x02013;1714.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8781233</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Kotzyba-Hibert, F., T. Grutter, and M. Goeldner. <year>1999</ye